Golden Carnivore Thanksgiving "Stuffing"

**Summary:** 
Browned pork and broth-soaked pork rinds baked under golden Parmesan. All the cozy comfort of Thanksgiving stuffing, no bread.

* **Difficulty:** Easy
* **Prep Time:** 15 minutes
* **Cook Time:** 55 minutes
* **Servings:** 8

### Nutrition Info (Per Serving)

| Calories | Protein | Fat | Carbs |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| 410 kcal | 28g | 32g | 1g |

---

### Ingredients

* **1 1/2 lb (680g) Ground pork**, plain and unseasoned (not sausage, which usually contains spices)
* **4 oz (113g) Plain pork rinds**, broken into rough, bite-size pieces (look for just pork skin and salt on the label)
* **3 Large eggs**, at room temperature
* **1 cup (240ml) Chicken bone broth**, made from only bones, water and salt
* **4 tbsp (57g) Salted butter**, divided
* **1 1/2 oz (43g) Parmesan cheese**, finely grated from the block (about 1/2 cup)
* **1/2 tsp Fine sea salt**, plus more to taste

---

### Instructions

1. **Prep the Oven:** Preheat your oven to **350°F (177°C)**. Rub **1 tbsp** of the butter over the inside of a 9x9-inch (or similar 2-quart) baking dish.
2. **Brown the Pork:** Set a large skillet over medium-high heat and add the ground pork. Break it into small crumbles and cook for **10–12 minutes**, until deeply browned with no pink remaining. Season with the salt, take the pan off the heat and let it cool for **5 minutes** so it won't scramble the eggs.
3. **Brown the Butter:** While the pork cools, melt the remaining **3 tbsp** of butter in a small saucepan over medium heat. Swirl the pan for **3–4 minutes**, until it smells nutty and the milk solids turn golden brown.
4. **Make the Custard:** In a large bowl, whisk the eggs and broth until smooth, then slowly whisk in the browned butter.
5. **Build the Stuffing:** Add the pork rinds and the browned pork, along with every drop of the pan drippings, to the bowl. Fold gently until every piece is coated. Let it sit for **5 minutes** so the rinds soak up the liquid and soften like bread.
6. **Bake:** Spread the mixture into the buttered dish and scatter the Parmesan over the top. Cover with foil and bake for **20 minutes**. Uncover and bake for another **15–20 minutes**, until the top is golden and crisp at the edges and the center reaches **165°F (74°C)** on an instant-read thermometer.
7. **Rest and Serve:** Let the stuffing rest for **5 minutes**, then spoon it out right next to your Thanksgiving turkey.

---

### Pro-Tip

Pork rinds stand in for the usual bread cubes here. Break them into rough, bite-size pieces instead of crushing them into crumbs so they soak up the broth and bake up soft and spoonable, just like classic stuffing.
